# stellar-contrib-board — project rules

## Scope

- Testnet only. No mainnet code paths, no network switcher.
- No smart contracts. This level is Stellar Classic payments only.
- No auth, no database, no wallet-kit abstraction layer. Freighter directly.

## Honesty constraints — these matter more than features

- Payouts are manual and trust the pot holder. Never describe the app as
  automated, trustless, or decentralized in code comments, UI copy, or the
  README.
- Contribution data is a point-in-time snapshot, not live. Label it as such
  wherever shown.
- Do not invent contributor Stellar addresses. Ever. An unmapped contributor
  renders as disabled.

## Error handling is the deliverable

Every failure path must be reachable and produce a distinct, readable message.
Prefer an explicit handled error over a silent catch or a generic toast. If you
find yourself writing `catch {}`, stop and handle it.

## Commits

Commit after each numbered build step, with a real message describing what
changed. Target 14–16 commits across the build. Never squash the history into a
single commit.
